ich included 493 independent contractor trucks; and 8,020 trailers. PAMT CORP was formerly known as P.A.M. Transportation Services, Inc., and changed its name to PAMT CORP in November 2024. The company was founded in 1980 and is headquartered in Tontitown, Arkansas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Lance K. Stewart | President, CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $590,590 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $253K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $232 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["PAMT CORP is a micro-cap industrials business with a $300M market cap on $598M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -14% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $23M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 13.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -3.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 5.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 77% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 20% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 1207% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":12.070392749244713},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Avis Budget Group (NASDAQ:CAR) and PAMT (NASDAQ:PAMT) Financial Comparison","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/avis-budget-group-nasdaqcar-and-pamt-nasdaqpamt-financial-comparison.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794571425.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Liquidity Mapping Around (PAMT) Price Events","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/149/Liquidity_Mapping_Around_PAMT_Price_Events_110626034002_1793997602.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793997602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title